# FretWise local song catalog — example / template
#
# This is an OFFLINE, user-editable metadata catalog. No network lookup is ever
# performed. Copy this file to "songs.tsv" (or any path) and point the web
# "index_path" setting at it. Edit by hand or export TSV from a spreadsheet.
#
# Format:
#   * Tab-separated values, UTF-8 (a leading BOM is fine).
#   * The first NON-COMMENT row below is the header naming the columns.
#   * Lines beginning with "#" here are documentation; the real catalog file you
#     create does not need them (DictReader will simply ignore unknown rows that
#     lack a key, but it is cleanest to start with the header row).
#
# Columns (all optional except the key):
#   filename  Key — the score filename, e.g. "Aerosmith - Back In The Saddle.gp".
#             Matched on the full name AND the extension-less stem, so either
#             works. Aliases: file / name / stem.
#   title     Song title.
#   artist    Performing artist / composer.
#   album     Album the track belongs to.
#   genre     Musical genre (also feeds the library Genre filter).
#   year      Release / recording year.
#   notes     Free-form notes (tuning, capo, difficulty, ...).
#
# Non-empty catalog values OVERRIDE values parsed from the filename. Anything
# you leave blank is filled in from the filename. album/genre/notes are only
# ever shown when you supply them here.
#
# The header row and two example rows below show the layout (replace them with
# your own data — do not commit your real catalog):
filename	title	artist	album	genre	year	notes
Aerosmith - Back In The Saddle - 10-16-2024.gp	Back in the Saddle	Aerosmith	Rocks	Hard Rock	1976	Drop D feel, watch the slide intro
Pink Floyd - Time.gp	Time	Pink Floyd	The Dark Side of the Moon	Progressive Rock	1973	Standard tuning; tasteful bends
